  "finding": "Fresh-process HiFi4/HiFi3 tests verify actual FP32 operand/accumulation configurations and bitwise input device roundtrips. The FP32 cancellation has exact CPU result1 but native result0 under both fidelities. BF16-representable cancellation gives2^-14 exactly under HiFi4 but zero under HiFi3. Random matmul outputs retain bits beyond ten fraction bits, ruling out a simple final-output-only quantization model. K1 rewrites to broadcast multiply and is exact on BF16-representable values; it is not evidence of exact matrix-unit arithmetic. General matrix errors differ across K32/K128 and fidelity; this does not locate every internal loss or quantify sampler contribution.",
  "tests": "Five CPU counterfactual/fresh-process guard checks pass. Each of16 native cases verifies bitwise input roundtrip, exact output repeats, no fallback and no aten counters. Native runtime IR proves three matmul graph shapes and one K1 broadcast-multiply graph per fidelity.",
  "decision": "Use verified matrix precision behavior when choosing an attention experiment. Input truncation and reduction arithmetic need separate controls; neither tensor dtype nor requested fidelity alone proves FP32 preservation. No model default or numerical gate changes.",
  "reproduce": "Run fp32_matmul_probe.py --math-fidelities hifi4 --output-dir <new> and hifi3 in two separate processes. Device lock serializes them; seed62 and inputs match. Archive retains raw reports, outputs, metrics and actual runtime IR."
}
